; The save checks of the generational collector, first session (contract G3
; step 2 revision 1, section 12, C14 and C25; README.md, save/): on a band of
; step 2 (E1's microcode, E3's band), with --files
; lisp/generational-collector.lisp,lisp/generational-collector-save.lisp
; (and a plant after them, if any); then the harness types
; (si:disk-save "LODn" t), whose save closes the connection, waits for the
; partition to hold a band of format 2020, and boots it for after.cases.
; Written with E2 and not yet run.  Its cases run in USER.

; collections off, now and at the saved band's boot; word 224 is 0, which
; DISK-SAVE requires
(gcsave-off) => T
(list si:gc-on si:gc-on-at-boot) => (NIL NIL)
(si:disk-save-refused-write-backs) => 0

; C14: a young list held only by a slot of a static array, on a page that is
; not its region's first; the BEFORE-COLD initialization for C14 (d) added
(gcsave-c14-setup) => (T T)

; C25: a young list held only by NIL's property list (a wired page), by the
; property list of a symbol between the band's wired size and 1000000 (a page
; wired for the restore), and C14's array above 1000000 (a paged page).  If
; (b) is NIL the layout has no symbol there: E4 picks another object or
; records that it has none (contract C25 (b))
(gcsave-c25-setup) => (T T T)
(and *gcsave-c25b-symbol* (si:%pointer-unsigned (%pointer *gcsave-c25b-symbol*)))

; the sums before the save; C14 (d)'s list is made by the save
(gcsave-sums) => (49995000 NIL 49995000 49995000)
